            "source": "cpu.edu.ph (Admission Requirements / Online Admission announcements). Requirements may change each school year; confirm with the CPU Information Center.",
            "body": "<p><strong>Requirements for incoming first-year students:</strong></p><ul><li>Senior High School Report Card (Form 138)</li><li>PSA-authenticated Birth Certificate</li><li>Certificate of Good Moral Character (optional)</li><li>2×2 ID picture</li></ul><p><strong>How to apply:</strong></p><ol><li>Pre-register online at registration.cpu.edu.ph</li><li>Pay the ₱500 admission fee through CPU's official payment options</li><li>Submit your requirements and wait for your admission confirmation</li><li>Proceed to enrollment and advising at the College of Business and Accountancy</li></ol><p>The CPU College Aptitude Test (CPUCAT) is currently required only for Engineering, Pharmacy and Medical Laboratory Science applicants, not for CBA programs.</p><p>Applicants without a final SHS report card yet may submit a scanned PSA birth certificate and Grade 12 ID.</p><p>CPU Information Center: (033) 329-1971 local 2129 · 0921 760 2647 · infocenter@cpu.edu.ph</p>"
