        "honors": {
          "type": "honors",
          "settings": {
            "title": "College Honors Policy",
            "source": "CBA Student Handbook, revised August 2024, effective School Year 2024-2025",
            "body": "<p><strong>Minimum study load.</strong> A prospective honor student must maintain a minimum study load of 18 units each semester or 6 units for the summer term, except when the curriculum prescribes otherwise. Working students (CPU work students or students employed full- or part-time) must carry the same minimum load. Non-CPU working students must submit Certificates of Employment to the Registrar's Office and the Dean's Office at the start of every term to justify any academic underload.</p><p><strong>Grade requirement.</strong> To qualify for honors, a college student must NOT have a grade lower than 2.0.</p><p><strong>Failing grade.</strong> A student with a failing (F) or 5.0 grade in any course, whether in a previous or current degree program and whether taken at CPU or another school, will be ineligible for academic honors.</p><p><strong>Dropped or left marks.</strong> A student with a dropped (D) or left (L) mark in any course, whether in a previous or current degree program and whether taken at CPU or another school, will be ineligible for academic honors.</p><p><strong>Incomplete grades.</strong> A student with an incomplete or lapsed incomplete mark on any required course taken from another school, or a lapsed incomplete on any required course taken at CPU, is disqualified for honors. A graduating student who fails to complete an INC before the date of deliberation has the application for graduation canceled for that term, disqualifying them from honors.</p>",
            "items": "Summa cum laude | 1.00 – 1.18\nMagna cum laude | 1.19 – 1.37\nCum laude | 1.38 – 1.56",
            "footer_rte": "<p><strong>Honors Point Average (HPA).</strong> HPA is computed from the prescribed courses of the curriculum, excluding SEAL and NSTP grades. For transfer students, only courses in the current curriculum and courses from another school duly approved by the college dean are included. If a required course is taken twice, the first grade is used. HPA = Sum of (Grade × Credit Units) ÷ Total Units.</p><p><strong>Residency at CPU.</strong> To qualify for honors, a student must have completed at CPU at least 75 percent of the total academic units required for graduation, and must have been enrolled for at least two years immediately before graduation.</p><p><strong>Years to complete the degree.</strong> To qualify for honors, a student must finish the degree program within the number of years required by the curriculum.</p><p><strong>Disciplinary action.</strong> After due process, a student found guilty of an offense and subject to disciplinary action will not be eligible to receive any academic honors.</p>"
          }
        }
